  "details": "In https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-feedback/p/fix-udon-security-vulnerability-illegal-network-function-calls-via-modded-client a recommendation was made to use method names starting with a _ to avoid network invocation, with a note that existing Udon method names were reserved. However it's unclear what will happen if Udon later introduces new callback method names that might conflict with custom event names being used in existing worlds. Please document a specific naming convention starting with _ that will never conflict with current or future reserved keywords.",
